BT /F2 16 Tf 56 762.8 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement - Remote Work and Code of Conduct \(HR-POL-07\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 720.7 Td (Remote Work and Code of Conduct Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 691.7 Td (Policy Number: HR-POL-07) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 677.2 Td (Version: 1.4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 662.7 Td (Effective Date: Immediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 648.2 Td (Applicability: Shore Staff, Kestrel Shipmanagement) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 606.2 Td (Introduction and Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 577.2 Td (This policy outlines the operational guidelines for remote work arrangements and establishes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 562.7 Td (the ethical standards expected of all shore staff at Kestrel Shipmanagement. As our) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 548.2 Td (organization continues to evolve, we recognize the importance of flexibility in how we work,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 533.7 Td (balanced against the need for accountability, security, and professional integrity. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 519.2 Td (document serves as the definitive reference for hybrid working arrangements, equipment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 504.7 Td (usage, ethical conduct, and grievance procedures. All employees are required to familiarize) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 490.2 Td (themselves with these guidelines to ensure compliance with company standards and local labor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 475.7 Td (regulations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 433.6 Td (Hybrid and Remote Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 404.6 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement supports a flexible work environment designed to enhance productivity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 390.1 Td (and work-life balance while maintaining strong team cohesion. The following rules govern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 375.6 Td (remote work eligibility and scheduling:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 346.6 Td (- Eligibility: Confirmed employees may work remotely up to 2 days per week, provided this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 332.1 Td (  arrangement is explicitly agreed upon with their manager. This agreement should be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 317.6 Td (  documented in the employee's file or shared calendar to ensure operational visibility.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 303.1 Td (- Probationary Period: Employees currently on probation are required to work from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 288.6 Td (  office exclusively. Remote work privileges are not available during this initial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 274.1 Td (  assessment phase to facilitate proper onboarding, mentorship, and cultural integration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 259.6 Td (- Managerial Approval: Any request for remote work must be discussed and approved by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 245.1 Td (  direct manager prior to implementation. Managers retain the right to deny remote work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 230.6 Td (  requests if business continuity or team collaboration requirements cannot be met.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 188.6 Td (Working Hours and Availability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 159.6 Td (To ensure seamless communication across teams and time zones, specific availability windows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 145.1 Td (are mandated for all shore staff, regardless of their physical location.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 116.1 Td (- Core Hours: The designated core hours are 10:00 to 16:00 IST. During this window, every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 101.6 Td (  employee must be reachable via standard company communication channels \(email, instant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 87.1 Td (  messaging, and phone\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement \(fictional company\) - HR-POL-07 v1.5 - page 1 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
