5 0 obj
<< /Length 3992 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 771.5 Td (- Responsiveness: Employees are expected to respond to urgent inquiries within a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (  reasonable timeframe during core hours. Failure to maintain availability during these) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (  specified times may be considered a breach of performance expectations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (- Flexibility Outside Core Hours: Work performed outside of core hours is permitted for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (  confirmed employees with prior managerial approval, provided that total working hours do) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 699.0 Td (  not exceed statutory limits and that rest periods are respected.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 656.9 Td (Equipment and Allowances) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 627.9 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement provides necessary tools to support remote work while ensuring data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 613.4 Td (security and operational efficiency. Financial allowances are also provided to offset the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 598.9 Td (costs associated with working from home.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 569.9 Td (- Internet Reimbursement: To support connectivity requirements, the company provides an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 555.4 Td (  internet reimbursement of INR 1,500 per month for remote work. This allowance is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 540.9 Td (  processed via payroll and requires employees to maintain valid proof of internet service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 526.4 Td (  payments if audited by the finance department.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 511.9 Td (- Company-L Provided Equipment: All necessary hardware, including laptops and peripherals,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 497.4 Td (  remains the property of Kestrel Shipmanagement. Employees are responsible for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 482.9 Td (  safekeeping of these items while working remotely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 468.4 Td (- Return of Assets: Company laptops must be returned within 7 days of the last working) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 453.9 Td (  day. This applies to both voluntary resignations and terminations. Failure to return) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 439.4 Td (  assets within this timeframe may result in deductions from final settlements or legal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 424.9 Td (  action to recover the equipment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 382.9 Td (Gifts and Hospitality) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 353.9 Td (To maintain objectivity and prevent undue influence, strict guidelines govern the acceptance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 339.4 Td (of gifts and hospitality from external parties.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 310.4 Td (- Vendor and Supplier Gifts: Employees may only accept gifts from vendors or suppliers if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 295.9 Td (  the value is no more than INR 2,000 per item. Any gift exceeding this threshold must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 281.4 Td (  declined politely and reported to the compliance team.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 266.9 Td (- Recording Requirements: Every accepted gift, regardless of value, must be recorded in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252.4 Td (  the official gift register. This log includes details such as the giver's name, date of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 237.9 Td (  receipt, description of the item, and estimated value. The register is subject to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 223.4 Td (  periodic audit by the internal audit department.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 208.9 Td (- Prohibited Items: Cash, cash equivalents, and gifts intended to influence business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 194.4 Td (  decisions are strictly prohibited under all circumstances.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 152.3 Td (Conflicts of Interest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 123.3 Td (Employees must act in the best interest of Kestrel Shipmanagement at all times. A conflict) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 108.8 Td (of interest arises when an employee's personal interests interfere, or appear to interfere,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 94.3 Td (with their professional duties.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement \(fictional company\) - HR-POL-07 v1.5 - page 2 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
