BT /F1 10 Tf 56 771.5 Td (- Confirmed Employees: The notice period for confirmed employees is 60 days. During this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (  period, the employee is expected to continue fulfilling their duties, assist in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (  knowledge transfer, and complete all exit formalities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (- Probationary Employees: For employees still on probation, the notice period is 15 days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (  This shorter duration reflects the preliminary nature of the employment relationship) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 699.0 Td (  during the initial assessment phase.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 684.5 Td (- Exit Formalities: All employees must complete an exit interview with HR and return all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 670.0 Td (  company property, including access cards, laptops, and documents, in accordance with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 655.5 Td (  timelines specified in this policy. Failure to adhere to notice periods may impact final) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 641.0 Td (  pay, experience letters, or future rehire eligibility.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 612.0 Td (*) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 583.0 Td (*This policy is subject to periodic review by the Human Resources department. Any updates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 568.5 Td (will be communicated to all shore staff via official company channels.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement \(fictional company\) - HR-POL-07 v1.5 - page 4 of 4) Tj ET
